    <briefdescription>
<para>GPU device discovery. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Enumerates physical GPU devices available to the process. When no real GPU runtime is present (or when the edition forbids GPU use) an empty list or a single CPU-fallback sentinel is returned so that callers never have to null-check.</para>
<sect1 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_device_discovery_1autotoc_md8_1s1"><sect2 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_device_discovery_1autotoc_md8">
<title>Design notes</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>All methods are static; there is no device handle or runtime state kept inside this class.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Real CUDA/ROCm integration is a future TODO guarded by THEMIS_ENABLE_CUDA / THEMIS_ENABLE_HIP compile-time defines.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Currently returns a CPU-fallback sentinel device when no GPU runtime is present, which lets the memory manager and safe-fail logic operate without hardware. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
